. Voting membership selects the majority order statistic (both majorities in joint mode); maybeCommit additionally requires the selected entry to have the current leader term. Append broadcasts propagate new commit, while heartbeats cap it by each follower Match. Followers check the previous entry and prevent committed-prefix overwrite. Ready exposes committed entries in order; snapshot and application quota can delay delivery. Caller application and Advance or async responses update application bookkeeping.', ['B-leadercommit','B-followerlog','B-durability','B-config','B-apply'],['F-commit','F-config','F-applied'])\ncontext=path('A promotable node without unapplied committed configuration changes can campaign. Pre-vote does not change term; real candidacy increments term and persists votes, and only current voting quorum support wins. Winning leadership resets follower progress, appends an empty entry and begins replication. Step normally relinquishes authority on higher term and rejects old replies; pre-vote and lease exceptions are explicit. Same-term leader messages displace candidates. CheckQuorum can step down. Transfer suppresses proposals until a caught-up voter receives TimeoutNow, with timeout abort and normal election safeguards. Removal can optionally step down the leader.', ['B-election','B-transfer','B-config','B-durability'],['F-authority','F-config'])\nconnection=path('Membership qualifies both election and replication support. Term resets discard old match/vote/readOnly acknowledgment tracking; Step rejects stale responses, while previously committed history remains binding. Entry stability acknowledgments retain the producing term to avoid discarding a replaced unstable suffix; old snapshot completions remain meaningful because snapshots carry committed state. Restart loads durable history/configuration and enters follower state. Pending pre-commit reads live separately from the reset readOnly queue and are released on response-based current-term commit. Applied membership may reinterpret existing matches and produce a commit without that same read-release callback. Application completion can propose automatic joint exit, but transfer admission can reject that proposal; these local continuation questions do not prevent understanding the backbone.', ['B-election','B-leadercommit','B-config','B-durability','B-recovery','B-apply','B-autoleave','B-read'],['F-authority','F-commit','F-config','F-applied'])\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go Raft library, including RawNode/Node, log, tracker, quorum, configuration and in-memory storage support. Network transport, actual durable storage and client state-machine work are caller owned.',protocol_contexts=['Per-node term and role','Per-node active and joint configuration','Log index/term prefix','Ordered Ready or async local storage streams'],external_interfaces=['RawNode/Node','Storage','Ready/Advance','MsgStorageAppend/Apply and attached responses'],ownership=['Node serializes state machine; RawNode caller must serialize','Caller supplies ticks, network delivery, persistence and ordered application'],variants=['PreVote','CheckQuorum','ReadOnlySafe/lease','AsyncStorageWrites','JointImplicit/Explicit','StepDownOnRemoval'],source_ids=['S-rawapi','S-nodeloop','S-nodecontract','S-storagecontract','S-storage'],unknowns=['External concrete transport and persistence implementations are not supplied']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.switchToConfig -> maybeCommit',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-config','B-read'],reason='Does legal application timing permit first-current-term commit here with pending reads, and what obligation survives explicit caller retry?',source_ids=['S-config','S-nodecontract','S-read-release']),dict(entry_point='raft.appliedTo -> Step while transferring',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-autoleave','B-transfer'],reason='Who retries automatic joint exit after transfer rejects it and later aborts without further application?',source_ids=['S-autoleave','S-proposal','S-abort','S-jointcontract'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='MemoryStorage and unstable ownership/compaction',disposition='deferred',reason='Read slice ownership and compaction/reconstruction mechanisms beyond their interface boundary.',source_ids=['S-storagecontract'],high_consequence=True)],core_overview=dict(formation=formation,context=context,connection=connection,status='usable',core_gaps=[],open_details=['Optimized early Advance and configuration application timing','Automatic joint exit retry following failed transfer','Detailed snapshot storage errors and compaction ownership','Read context queue lifecycle across term changes'],rationale='Representative formation, authority, old-work handling, configuration, persistence, recovery and consumption paths are sourced; local continuation and ownership questions remain explicit rather than asserted as defects.'))\njson.dump(m,open('core-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='When an applied implicit joint configuration owes automatic exit and its internal leave proposal is rejected during leadership transfer, does transfer abort restore an implementation-owned continuation without an unrelated client proposal?',importance='A stranded joint configuration would retain the outgoing quorum requirement and can obstruct subsequent membership changes; no safety violation or global unavailability has been demonstrated.',source_ids=['S-autoleave','S-proposal','S-abort','S-ticks','S-jointcontract','S-nodecontract'],participants=['Current leader','Transfer target','Incoming and outgoing voters','Application driver'],objects=['AutoLeave configuration','Internal zero ConfChangeV2 proposal','Applied cursor','leadTransferee'],contexts=['Implicit joint configuration on a leader','Transfer active when committed configuration application completes','Transfer timeout with continued viable joint quorum'],event_paths=['ApplyConfChange -> application completion -> appliedTo -> Step(MsgProp) -> transfer rejection','tickHeartbeat -> abortLeaderTransfer -> ordinary heartbeat/response activity'],activity_classes=['A4','A2','A1'],behavior_ids=['B-config','B-autoleave'],fact_ids=['F-config'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-transfer':'Establishes rejection interval and clears it on timeout','B-apply':'Supplies application-completion trigger and caller ordering','B-leadercommit':'Commits joint and leave entries under voter requirements'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['appliedTo retries on each subsequently applied entry; a successful transfer may elect a leader whose empty entry supplies another trigger','External proposals may be lost and retried by callers, so responsibility for the internally generated automatic proposal must be distinguished','No legal execution or complete suffix trigger analysis has yet been performed'],unknowns=['Can legal Ready application overlap an active transfer at exactly this trigger?','Does any timer, heartbeat, configuration callback or queued application acknowledgment independently retry after abort?','What continuation responsibility follows from implicit-transition API semantics under a stable leader and available joint quorum?'],trigger_rationale='appliedTo explicitly anticipates transfer rejection and says a later advance retries; abortLeaderTransfer only clears the field and synchronous Advance invokes appliedTo only for actual application work. A small controlled schedule can discriminate an independent retry from reliance on unrelated traffic after source review closes the trigger set.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\ns=dict(action='continue',rationale='Register the sourced two-line core map and investigate a distinct automatic-configuration continuation premise. The read question remains a surface; no liveness obligation is inferred from a finite wait.',sources=sources,map_path='core-map.json',question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S-nodecontract','S-readycontract','S-autoleave','S-abort','S-jointcontract'],answered='ReadIndex explicitly permits unnoticed loss and requires caller retry, so missing read completion by itself is not a grounded violation. The Ready interface requires Entries persisted before synchronous Messages, which is stricter than the README same-batch overlap wording; a future driver can obey both by persisting before send. Automatic joint exit is separately promised by the configuration API and is initiated by appliedTo; transfer rejection and retry ownership therefore merit their own question.',remaining=['Read configuration-commit legal history, including documented early Advance, remains open without a completion claim','For automatic joint exit, close trigger coverage and execute a legal transfer/application overlap before fixing any obligation'],understanding='updated',rationale='Caller contracts narrow the original reading question; separate API semantics supply a more specific continuation discriminator.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_map.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_19-14-52-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-map.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
