rt. Voting membership selects the majority order statistic (both majorities in joint mode); maybeCommit additionally requires the selected entry to have the current leader term. Append broadcasts propagate new commit, while heartbeats cap it by each follower Match. Followers check the previous entry and prevent committed-prefix overwrite. Ready exposes committed entries in order; snapshot and application quota can delay delivery. Caller application and Advance or async responses update application bookkeeping.', ['B-leadercommit','B-followerlog','B-durability','B-config','B-apply'],['F-commit','F-config','F-applied'])\ncontext=path('A promotable node without unapplied committed configuration changes can campaign. Pre-vote does not change term; real candidacy increments term and persists votes, and only current voting quorum support wins. Winning leadership resets follower progress, appends an empty entry and begins replication. Step normally relinquishes authority on higher term and rejects old replies; pre-vote and lease exceptions are explicit. Same-term leader messages displace candidates. CheckQuorum can step down. Transfer suppresses proposals until a caught-up voter receives TimeoutNow, with timeout abort and normal election safeguards. Removal can optionally step down the leader.', ['B-election','B-transfer','B-config','B-durability'],['F-authority','F-config'])\nconnection=path('Membership qualifies both election and replication support. Term resets discard old match/vote/readOnly acknowledgment tracking; Step rejects stale responses, while previously committed history remains binding. Entry stability acknowledgments retain the producing term to avoid discarding a replaced unstable suffix; old snapshot completions remain meaningful because snapshots carry committed state. Restart loads durable history/configuration and enters follower state. Pending pre-commit reads live separately from the reset readOnly queue and are released on response-based current-term commit. Applied membership may reinterpret existing matches and produce a commit without that same read-release callback. Application completion can propose automatic joint exit, but transfer admission can reject that proposal; these local continuation questions do not prevent understanding the backbone.', ['B-election','B-leadercommit','B-config','B-durability','B-recovery','B-apply','B-autoleave','B-read'],['F-authority','F-commit','F-config','F-applied'])\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go Raft library, including RawNode/Node, log, tracker, quorum, configuration and in-memory storage support. Network transport, actual durable storage and client state-machine work are caller owned.',protocol_contexts=['Per-node term and role','Per-node active and joint configuration','Log index/term prefix','Ordered Ready or async local storage streams'],external_interfaces=['RawNode/Node','Storage','Ready/Advance','MsgStorageAppend/Apply and attached responses'],ownership=['Node serializes state machine; RawNode caller must serialize','Caller supplies ticks, network delivery, persistence and ordered application'],variants=['PreVote','CheckQuorum','ReadOnlySafe/lease','AsyncStorageWrites','JointImplicit/Explicit','StepDownOnRemoval'],source_ids=['S-rawapi','S-nodeloop','S-nodecontract','S-storagecontract','S-storage'],unknowns=['External concrete transport and persistence implementations are not supplied']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.switchToConfig -> maybeCommit',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-config','B-read'],reason='Does legal application timing permit first-current-term commit here with pending reads, and what obligation survives explicit caller retry?',source_ids=['S-config','S-nodecontract','S-read-release']),dict(entry_point='raft.appliedTo -> Step while transferring',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-autoleave','B-transfer'],reason='Who retries automatic joint exit after transfer r